# UI/UX Design Principles (No AI-template Look)

- Core stack: always prioritize `shadcn/ui` components (`Button`, `Card`, `Badge` etc.) before custom primitive markup.
- Typography: keep global base in `font-serif` (Source Serif 4 + Noto Serif JP). H1/H2 must use `tracking-tight` and `leading-none` or `leading-tight` for editorial weight.
- Dark theme strategy: avoid neon accents; use refined zinc/slate palette (`bg-zinc-950`, `text-zinc-100`, `text-zinc-300`) with minimal accent usage.
- Whitespace-first layout: primary sections should breathe (`py-24` to `py-32`, generous vertical rhythm). Avoid cramped spacing patterns.
- Surface treatment: avoid heavy default shadows and obvious borders; use subtle borders (`border-zinc-800` / translucent) and minimal soft shadows only when needed.
- Badge/label hierarchy: small labels (e.g. BETA) should be `uppercase` with `tracking-widest` to create typographic contrast against large serif headlines.

